<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO begins trading ex-share split.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO begins trading ex-share split.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ABN AMRO NV opened at 35.10 guilders on the first day of trading after the Dutch bank's four-for-one share split.</p>
<p>At 0740 GMT, the shares were trading on the Amsterdam bourse at 34.80 guilders, compared with a close of 138.20 on Monday, the last day before the split became effective.</p>
<p>The shares see-sawed on Tuesday on speculation ahead of the share split, aimed at increasing liquidity in the shares.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
